      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ تَكُونُ مَعِيَ اَلدَّرَاهِمُ فِيهَا تَمَاثِيلُ وَ أَنَا مُحْرِمٌ فَأَجْعَلُهَا فِي هِمْيَانِي وَ أَشُدُّهُ فِي وَسَطِي قَالَ «لاَ بَأْسَ أَوَ لَيْسَ هِيَ نَفَقَتَكَ وَ عَلَيْهَا اِعْتِمَادُكَ بَعْدَ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2449 - Ali ibn Asbat narrated from his uncle Ya‘qub ibn Salim, who said:\nI said to Abu Abdullah (as), \"I have coins with images on them while I am in a state of Ihram. I place them in my belt and tie it around my waist. Is this permissible?\"\nImam (as) said: \"There is no problem with that. Are they not your expenses upon which you rely after Allah (swt), the Mighty and Glorious?\""
        ]
      }
